  "designNotes": "A rock wall with a single gap forces both lines onto one belt: merge, then split with a sorter (iron takes the sorter's forward lane, so copper gets the lane that can reach the far-left demand without crossing). Rocks make the obvious \"smelt each ore at its source\" plan awkward: the reference smelts iron after the sorter (direct link into the demand, cheaper), while the alternate detours iron through a bent belt above the wall for a smaller footprint at +1 cost.",
